 r←Test_Misc_034(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;folder;report;matrix
⍝ Exercise `GetGitStatusReport` on a repository without any commits - the branch that reports
⍝ "Nothing has been commited yet". Only a project opened with batch←0 ever gets there.\\
⍝ The report is displayed with `↑`, so every item must be a simple character vector. An item of a
⍝ different depth is not shown as a line at all: it is spread out one character per column, and it
⍝ pads the whole report to its own length. That is what `1 G.Status` returning a one-column matrix
⍝ once did to this report, and what no test noticed.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 r←T._Failed

 :If ~##.Cider.G.IsGitInstalled
     r←T._NotApplicable ⋄ →0
 :EndIf

 folder←∆GetFolderInTempDir'Test_Misc_034'
 {}1 ##.Cider.G.Init folder
 →T.GoToTidyUp~##.Cider.G.IsGitProject folder

 report←##.Cider.GetGitStatusReport folder

⍝ Simple character vectors throughout: an empty line is depth 0, anything nested would be 2 or more
 →T.GoToTidyUp~∧/1≥≡¨report
 →T.GoToTidyUp~∧/{' '=1↑0⍴⍵}¨report

⍝ ... so that mixing them yields a character matrix rather than a nested one
 matrix←↑report
 →T.GoToTidyUp~2=⍴⍴matrix
 →T.GoToTidyUp~' '=1↑0⍴matrix

⍝ The branch under test
 →T.GoToTidyUp~∨/∨/¨'Nothing has been commited yet'∘⍷¨report

 r←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 :Trap 0
     {}F.RmDirByForce folder
 :EndTrap
⍝Done
